# Beads/Dolt tool-managed data — config.yaml, metadata.json, issues.jsonl,
# PRIME.md, formulas, identity are written/rewritten by the beads CLI, not
# Prettier. Checking them makes `format:check` (and CI) fail whenever the
# tooling rewrites them unformatted.
.beads/
# Polecat per-bead git worktrees: untracked, 0 tracked files, and absent on
# clean CI checkouts. Without this, `prettier --check .` recursively scans
# every nested worktree — each a full repo copy — producing false
# `format:check`/`ci:local` failures and near-hangs in agent home worktrees.
worktrees/
# Gas City molecule scratch — untracked build artifacts and per-bead work dirs
# written into shared agent home worktrees, absent on clean CI checkouts.
# Without these, `prettier --check .` flags the generated Markdown and per-bead
# files as unformatted, producing false `format:check`/`ci:local` failures.
plans/
/ac-*/
# Gas City / agent tooling scratch written into shared rig checkouts. Every
# path here is untracked and absent on a clean CI checkout; without them
# `prettier --check .` flags them and `format:check`/`ci:local` fail for
# reasons unrelated to the change under test. Anchored with a leading slash:
# each is repo-root scratch, so an unanchored pattern would also shadow a
# same-named path nested anywhere in the tree.
/.codex/
/.playwright-mcp/
/apicity/
/schemas/
/packs.lock
/ref2video-*.json
# `.agents/` is TRACKED (hooks.json, rules/**, skills/beads/**), so a blanket
# `.agents/` ignore would silently drop shipped files from the gate. Only the
# gc-managed entries are excluded: the ownership manifest, and the
# `<pack>.<skill>` directories the skill vendor materializes. Tracked
# `skills/beads/` has no dot in its name, so `*.*/` cannot reach it. The
# discriminator keys on the dot in both directions: a gc-managed skill
# directory named without a dot would not be matched here and would re-break
# `format:check`.
/.agents/skills/.gc-skill-ownership.json
/.agents/skills/*.*/
